WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
How is your modified Pearson different than the traditional Gerson?

00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:10,800
So the traditional Gerson protocol is to do 13 glasses of juice every day.

00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:19,040
So basically a glass of juice every week you know or for the most part doing five coffee

00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:24,240
animals a day and then there's some nutritional pieces that were added to that too.

00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:31,600
Gerson is from Max Gerson who wrote several very good books on cancer and highly recommend them.

00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:40,800
But remember all his work with cancer patients was done back in the 1930s and 40s and 50s.

00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:47,200
Charlotte has kept up his work on a marvelous basis. Well we have found with a Gerson protocol

00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,560
first of all it can be juicing okay juicing and doing a Gerson protocol can be really good if your

00:00:54,560 --> 00:01:00,720
cancer is not fed through glycolysis. So if it is fed through glycolysis if you're

00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:08,480
juicing and care juicing it's very high in nutrient value but it's also very high in glucose.

00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:14,880
So you can't really do a Gerson type protocol if your cancer is fed mainly through glycolysis.

00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:21,840
The other issue that we have with Gerson is that it becomes very difficult to follow.

00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:30,880
So we've had patients come in the office literally balling in tears that they feel so ashamed

00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:35,680
that they cannot continue their Gerson protocol that they started prior to coming to us.

00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:43,760
So can a Gerson protocol full protocol juicing 13 glasses a day doing five coffee

00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:49,920
out of us be helpful. Yes I don't see that as real sustainable. You almost have to hire a maid

00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:56,160
or have multiple extended family members, gooey grocery shopping for you, juicing for you,

00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:02,240
just the physical ability to do that it limits everything else in life and if that's the last

00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:10,800
you know Hail Mary pass that we have to try to save life that's great and to do that for a period

00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:17,040
of time that might be necessary and it might be appropriate but in our clinic and in my life I'm

00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:27,120
trying to balance you know healing with respect for that person and respect for the quality of

00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:39,040
life they have. To me it's real easy to make an idol out of your healing if you are consumed with

00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:45,440
the tasks that you have to do in a given day to hopefully heal from the cancer and doing a full

00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:52,960
Gerson protocol can be life-consuming and it kind of defeats the purpose of why you want to heal the

00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:58,560
cancer so that you can live life if you can't live life. Now I understand if I have to do this for three

00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:05,040
months and this is going to give me another 10 years of life well going to say for all let's do

00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:12,160
the three months of doing Gerson but it's not everybody that has that experience it could just be

00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:18,240
draining on their life so it can be a good program for people it's not a good program for everybody

00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:24,000
just like anything else and we want to make sure that we're not consumed and make an idol out of our

00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,600
here or healing.

